From f6ea9a77a6916c51160abc4397bd22dc74ef221d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 19:50:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(deepseek-v4.1): prefill sequence-parallel state and
 embedding reduce-scatter

Stage 1 of a prefill-only sequence-parallel mode for TP > 1. With
SPARK3_DS41_PREFILL_SP_MIN_ROWS set, DeepseekV4Model.forward decides per
forward from the token count T (every rank shares it) whether to use SP,
never under CED compaction, pipeline parallelism, static sequence
parallelism or request boundary checkpoints, and never for decode-sized
forwards: the threshold is raised above the CUDA graph sizes and
max_num_seqs * (1 + num_speculative_tokens).

The vocabulary-parallel embedding reduce-scatters its masked partial rows
from a zero-padded buffer of Tp = TP * ceil(T / TP) rows. Each token has one
owning shard, so the sum is exact; this stage gathers the rows straight back,
so the forward is bit-identical to SP off while exercising the padding,
collectives and row layout. The static _use_sequence_parallel flag stays off
and no module or weight changes.
